00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:13.110
to add a scalar parameter

234
00:15:13.110 --> 00:15:16.419
that I'm going to call emissive strength.

235
00:15:17.610 --> 00:15:19.929
And I'm going to put a real high value

236
00:15:19.929 --> 00:15:21.929
because I want to make this real visible,

237
00:15:21.929 --> 00:15:23.289
and then I'm going to connect it to the D.

238
00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:28.409
Okay, so now if we plug the multiply node into the emissive,

239
00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:34.440
boom, you can see our final magical and parallax material.

240
00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:37.799
Now, if I zoom in a lot into this material,

241
00:15:37.799 --> 00:15:41.240
you start seeing this spherical artifact happening,

242
00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:45.190
and this is really dictated by two main values,

243
00:15:46.179 --> 00:15:48.500
the interior tiling and the height.

244
00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:51.860
So if I switch the height to something like 0.4,

245
00:15:51.940 --> 00:15:54.580
you can see that that's not happening anymore,

246
00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:59.590
but we start seeing these weird artifacts on the edges.

247
00:15:59.590 --> 00:16:01.509
So you really need to tweak these values

248
00:16:01.509 --> 00:16:02.389
a little bit around

249
00:16:02.389 --> 00:16:05.750
until you find the right balance of what you want.

250
00:16:06.740 --> 00:16:09.539
All right, I hope you enjoyed this class,

251
00:16:09.539 --> 00:16:10.500
and in the next video,

252
00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:14.419
we'll be looking into advanced glass node effects

253
00:16:14.419 --> 00:16:15.139
and techniques.

254
00:16:15.779 --> 00:16:16.500
I'll see you there.

255
00:16:17.059 --> 00:16:17.700
Bye.
